    <bpmn:process id="W_W3828" name="W3828. Assessor Qualification, Standardization &amp; Calibration" isExecutable="false">
      <bpmn:documentation>Trigger: Assessment cycle (W3819); standards drift
Frequency: Maintained + periodic
Volume: Assessor pool
Owner: Trade Capability / Quality / Compliance
Participants: Trade Capability, Quality (links to VS-31), Compliance (links to VS-22), L&amp;D (links to VS-19.4), Master Tradespersons/Assessors, TESDA (links to W3811)
Source: workflow W3828 — Assessor Qualification, Standardization &amp; Calibration</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:laneSet id="W3828_LaneSet2">
        <bpmn:lane id="W3828_Lane1" name="Trade Capability">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W3828_Task4</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W3828_Task5</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W3828_Task6</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W3828_Start3</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W3828_End7</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
      </bpmn:laneSet>
      <bpmn:startEvent id="W3828_Start3" name="Assessment cycle (W3819); standards drift">
        <bpmn:outgoing>W3828_Flow10</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:startEvent>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W3828_Task4" name="Trade Capability/Quality qualify assessors per standard: assessor qualification…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 1: Trade Capability/Quality qualify assessors per standard: assessor qualification (TESDA-accredited where applicable — links to W3811), assessment criteria training, and authorization to assess specific trades/competencies
Responsible (R): Trade Capability / Quality / Compliance
Accountable (A): Trade Capability Lead
Duration: Maintained</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W3828_Flow10</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W3828_Flow11</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W3828_Task5" name="Trade Capability/Quality run assessor calibration and standardization: regular…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 2: Trade Capability/Quality run assessor calibration and standardization: regular calibration sessions, moderation of scoring, double-scoring samples, and bias control so assessments are consistent across assessors/stores/regions
Responsible (R): Trade Capability / Quality
Accountable (A): Trade Capability Lead
Duration: Periodic</bpmn:documentation>
